els representing the crop rows. Thus, we deﬁne the crop volume factor as the number of pixels with green value higher than γh, i.e. α =| P>γh |. (17) Hereby, |P>γh | is actually an indicator of the crop volume factor α, and |P>γh | can be easily obtained with any given image. Notice, when the brightness level is the same, α is determined by the age of the crops since sprout. However this 